zebra: do not reuse an NHG that keeps a nexthop its owner removed

When a route's nexthop goes inactive with its interface and the owning
protocol then re-sends the route without that nexthop, zebra compared the
new group with the old one while skipping the old group's inactive
members, found them equal, and kept the old group. The removed nexthop
stayed in the route, and zebra installed it again as soon as its
interface came back up, forwarding onto a path the protocol had withdrawn
(FRRouting/frr#22752). An eBGP ECMP route resurrected this way sends
traffic to a peer whose session is not even established.

Skip an inactive old nexthop only together with the same nexthop in the
new group, so the old group is reused only when the owner still carries
every one of its nexthops.

--- a/zebra/zebra_nhg.c
+++ b/zebra/zebra_nhg.c
@@ -3073,8 +3073,12 @@
 					   __func__, rn);
 
 			/*
-			 * If the new nexthop is not active and the old nexthop is also not active,
-			 * then we know that we can skip both the old and new nexthops.
+			 * An inactive old nexthop can be skipped only together
+			 * with the same, equally inactive nexthop in the new
+			 * group. One the new group no longer carries was
+			 * removed by its owner, and reusing the old group would
+			 * keep it, to be installed again once its interface
+			 * comes back up.
 			 */
 			if (!CHECK_FLAG(nhop->flags, NEXTHOP_FLAG_ACTIVE) &&
 			    nexthop_same_no_ifindex(nhop, old_nhop)) {
@@ -3082,9 +3086,11 @@
 					zlog_debug("%s: %pRN new is not active going to the next one",
 						   __func__, rn);
 				nhop = nhop->next;
+				old_nhop = old_nhop->next;
+				continue;
 			}
-			old_nhop = old_nhop->next;
-			continue;
+			same = false;
+			break;
 		}
 
 		if (nexthop_same(nhop, old_nhop)) {
@@ -3135,18 +3141,8 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	if (nhop)
+	if (nhop || old_nhop)
 		same = false;
-	else if (old_nhop) {
-		while (old_nhop) {
-			if (CHECK_FLAG(old_nhop->flags, NEXTHOP_FLAG_ACTIVE))
-				break;
-			old_nhop = old_nhop->next;
-		}
-
-		if (old_nhop)
-			same = false;
-	}
 
 	return same;
 }
